.Dd March 13, 2026
.Dt FLOPPY 4
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm floppy
.Nd ISA floppy disk controller and drive support
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Cd "device floppy"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
driver supports NEC uPD765 and Intel 82077AA compatible floppy disk
controllers on the ISA bus.
Detected drives are published as block devices under
.Pa /dev/storage/fd0
and
.Pa /dev/storage/fd1 .
.Pp
The driver probes legacy controllers at:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Li 0x3F0 / IRQ 6
primary controller
.It Li 0x370 / IRQ 10
secondary controller
.El
.Pp
Drive geometry is selected from CMOS register
.Li 0x10
for the first two drives.
Supported media profiles include 360K, 720K, 1.2M, 1.44M, and 2.88M formats.
.Pp
Transfers use ISA DMA channel 2 through a low-memory bounce buffer below
16MB.
The current implementation performs sector I/O through CHS translation and
retries failed transfers after recalibration.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/dev/storage/fd0"
.It Pa /dev/storage/fd0
first floppy drive
.It Pa /dev/storage/fd1
second floppy drive
.El
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
The driver logs controller initialization failures, recalibration failures,
and transfer status-byte decodes with the
.Li fdc:
prefix.
.Sh BUGS
Reset completion still uses a settle-delay path instead of a strict reset IRQ
handshake.
Format-track commands, disk-change detection, and full four-drive support are
not implemented yet.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ide 4 ,
.Xr scsi 4
